cinematic universe  they go on to say that a source close to  bozeman tells the hollywood reporter  that the 43 year old actor  who had become noticeably thin in recent  months was convinced  until about a week before his death that  he was going to beat cancer and would be  able to gain the weight back for a black  panther sequel  that was scheduled to go into production  in march the actor was even set to  prepare  for the new film beginning in september  so it's just truly heartbreaking to hear  that chadwick thought that he was going  to be able to  actually film black panther 2 when he  thought that he was going to be able to  beat cancer  and it's understandable and admirable  people do it all the time and he's a  tough  guy he filmed so many different projects  while he was battling cancer and he  didn't tell anybody  kevin feige the president of marvel  studios didn't even know  until chadwick unfortunately passed away  now the article goes on to talk about  how  chadwick and black panther was a huge  part of the marvel cinematic universe  not only from what we've seen so far  but the future as well and when the  hollywood reporter asked disney  what their plans were right now what  they're focusing on and how they're  handling his death  disney sources said that the company is  processing its grief  and that its focus at this stage is to  pay tribute to bozeman and not on the  making of a black panther sequel  so rightfully so right now marvel  studios and disney is not focused on  black panther 2. they're not focused on  what do we do do we replace him do we  have shuri become the new black panther  they're not focused on that right now  if we've learned anything about chadwick  over this past week  since he passed was that he was an  amazing person and clearly meant  the world to a ton of people over at the  studio so right now they're not focused  on the loss of somebody who played a  character they're focused on the loss of  an amazing person  and it's 